     }\n        }\n        solve(bi, bj, mat[bi*n+bj], false);\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n                if (a[i][j] >= '1' && a[i][j] <= '9') {\n                    solve(i, j, mat[i*n+j], true);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        build();\n        System.out.println(edmondsKarp(2+n*n+n*n, 0, 1));\n    }\n\n    static void solve(int A, int B, int[] vis, boolean check) {\n        Queue<int[]> que = new LinkedList<>();\n        vis[A*n+B] = 0;\n        que.add(new int[]{A, B});\n        while (!que.isEmpty()) {\n            int[] now = que.poll();\n            int p = now[0]*n+now[1];\n            int dis = vis[p];\n            if (check && (mat[bi*n+bj][p] <= dis || t <= dis)) {\n                if (mat[bi*n+bj][p] < dis || t < dis) vis[p] = INF+1;\n                continue;\n            }\n            for (int d = 0; d < 4; d++) {\n                int i = dir[d][0]+now[0];\n                int j = dir[d][1]+now[1];\n                if (i < 0 || j < 0 || i == n || j == n) continue;\n                if (b[i][j] < '0' || b[i][j] > '9') continue;\n                int q = i*n+j;\n                if (vis[q] != INF) continue;\n                vis[q] = dis+1;\n                que.add(new int[]{i, j});\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    static void build() {\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n                if (b[i][j] <= '0' || b[i][j] > '9') continue;\n                ca.add(i);\n                cb.add(j);\n                int p = i*n+j;\n                cap[p+2+n*n][1] = b[i][j]-'0';\n            }\n        }\n        int z = bi*n+bj;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n                if (a[i][j] <= '0' || a[i][j] > '9') continue;\n                int p = i*n+j;\n                cap[0][p+2] = a[i][j]-'0';\n                for (int k = 0; k < ca.size(); k++) {\n                    int ii = ca.get(k);\n                    int jj = cb.get(k);\n                    int q = ii*n+jj;\n                    if (mat[p][q] < INF)\n                        cap[p+2][q+2+n*n] = INF;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    static int edmondsKarp(int n, int source, int sink) {\n        int p, q, t, i, j;\n        while (true) {\n            Arrays.fill(pre, -1);\n            d[source] = INF;\n            p = q = 0;\n            que[q++] = source;\n            while (p < q && pre[sink] < 0) {\n                t = que[p++];\n                for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n                    if (pre[i] < 0 && (j = cap[t][i] - flow[t][i]) > 0) {\n                        pre[que[q++] = i] = t;\n                        d[i] = Math.min(d[t], j);\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            if (pre[sink] < 0) break;\n            for (i = sink; i != source; i = pre[i]) {\n                flow[pre[i]][i] += d[sink];\n                flow[i][pre[i]] -= d[sink];\n            }\n        }\n        int j = 0;\n        for (i = 0; i < n; i++) j += flow[source][i];\n        return j;\n    }\n}\n\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.012815027497708797, -0.11482938379049301, -0.006640154868364334, -0.00022635281493421644, -0.47513532638549805, -0.459879606962204, -8.737658936297521e-05, -8.106198947643861e-06, -3.349725011503324e-05, -3.814624506048858e-05, -0.13541284203529358, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, -2.0146166207268834e-05, -1.3112935448589269e-05, -0.0028166405390948057, -0.0010336062405258417, -7.271502545336261e-05, -2.2291887944447808e-05, -0.694638192653656, -1.161984920501709, -0.02220541052520275, -5.722029527532868e-06, -0.029607383534312248, -0.3926490843296051, -0.07815896719694138, -0.14090122282505035, -0.4175857603549957, -0.6258517503738403, -0.0010521834483370185, -1.3351351299206726e-05, -0.0024996723514050245, -0.014771378599107265, -5.6980417866725475e-05, -0.0020183